Z||000007||Shiner||10-19-1999||11:38 PM||||I have about in inch and a half of headroom in my '87GT with sunroof, but I am 6'3", and built like a tank.  I would NOT be able to fit in that car PERIOD.  The fier is actually a very roomy sports car for big people.  I sat in a '99 BMW M coupe, and had about an inch of negative headroom. It sure was nice though, I never felt shift linkage that was so smooth.  I sure wish that there was a way to put a Porsche or a BMW 5 speed in a fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||10-20-1999||01:27 AM||||That is without a doubt the best looking car that I have seen.  I just love that look..<P>They don't do anything to the windshield, that would be way to expensive.. they just lay it back.  of course, $3,000 isn't too cheap, either..  ||||reg||14
Z||000009||VISCERAL||10-20-1999||01:52 AM||||Saw the car in person. It's not as detailed as you think. You gotta remember this was his test mule. Paint was rough and I wasn't sure the window fully closed properly, and the seams didn't mesh perfect. He's great with mechanical precision but not a stickler for aesthetic detail. That's his daily driver.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pretender||10-20-1999||03:19 AM||||it is a bad ass car! I read about it at archies website a while back. The windshield is stock but the rear and side windows were special made. ||||reg||10
Z||000011||87GTBro||10-20-1999||01:57 PM||||I heard V8-Archie is 6'4" and he fits in it fine.<BR>I personally love the look.  I am 6'1" and if I had the dough, I'd do it.<BR>There is also a .avi file of this car somewhere on the internet.  A movie of it taking off from inside a garage leaving a cloud of smoke as the tires drew parallel lines all the way out!  Hold on, I have it,<BR>Here it is: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/tx3/87GTBro/images/320C1.avi" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/tx3/87GTBro/images/320C1.avi</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 87GTBro (edited 10-20-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||10-20-1999||04:30 PM||||I have copies of those AVIs as well.. pretty cool.<BR>I agree, the chop-top is a very awesome car. When I first saw it last year (I think it was last year.. maybe early this year.) I remember thinking "I want one!!!!!".. if only <BR>1. I could afford it<BR>2. was a bit smaller! <P>still, sweet car.. the rear window is a del sol type, if I remember correctly.. sliding glass. The hood scoops were also a conversion that Archie was selling, but it's not listed on his site anymore as far as I can tell.||||reg||1
